'''''Spergularia villosa''''' is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Caryophyllaceae]] known by the common name '''hairy sandspurry'''.<ref>{{PLANTS|id=SPVI|taxon=Spergularia villosa|accessdate=25 November 2015}}</ref> It is native to southern South America, and it is known in the southwestern United States and [[Baja California]] as an [[introduced species]] and casual [[weed]]. It grows in a wide variety of habitat types. It is a small perennial herb producing a sprawling stem up to {{Convert|30|cm|sp=us}} long with a woody base. It is coated in glandular hairs. The leaves are generally linear in shape and measure a few centimeters long. They are accompanied by dull white lance-shaped [[stipule]]s. The flowers have hairy, glandular [[sepal]]s and five oval whitish petals.

